      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not necessary. t-\u003eto_proc is set when transaction is created and only transitions to NULL if the corresponding thread is released. Since it is safe to deref the proc, it really doesn\u0027t matter if we get a non-NULL proc and t-\u003eto_proc goes to NULL -- in this case t-\u003ebuffer-\u003etransaction will be written to NULL twice (here and in thread release) which is harmless. If we ever get NULL here, then we know t-\u003ebuffer-\u003etransaction was written to NULL.",
